+# Breadth: the effect regime
+
+```{r breadth-setup}
+.L <- function(s) readRDS(file.path(.dev, sprintf("oc_breadth_ladder_2026-08-30_%s.rds", s)))
+L0 <- .L("gate"); .rungs <- c(60, 80, 100, 120, 140, 160)
+LR <- lapply(.rungs, function(q) .L(sprintf("rung%d", q))); names(LR) <- .rungs
+FC <- .L("forecast120")
+S2 <- readRDS(file.path(.dev, "oc_breadth_stage2_2026-08-31_score.rds"))
+stopifnot(FC$q == 120, identical(S2$c1_star, FC$c1_star), S2$forecast_commit == "c9cb0ca2")
+.fr <- FC$star$resample; .fs <- FC$star$split; .fn <- FC$null_at_star
+```
+
+The ladder keeps the MD40 population and its true region `Q` and moves only
+`k_inter`, so that the oriented `Q` effect `q = |m_tau[Q]|` runs
+`r min(.rungs)`–`r max(.rungs)` against MD40's `r .f(abs(L0$m_tau[["Q"]]), 0)`
+(`k_inter(q) = k40 + s·(q − 40)`, `k40` = `r .f(L0$k40, 4)`, `s` = `r L0$s`);
+`|m_tau[Qc]|` = `r .f(abs(L0$m_tau[["Qc"]]), 3)` is unchanged on every rung.
+Because the family, `Pg`, `PQg`, `se_g` and the overlap are functions of
+`df_super`'s covariates and `Q` alone, they are `identical()` across rungs and
+**only `beta_g = tauQc + bint(q)·PQg` moves**; the draw set (`r .fm(C$draws)`
+draws, seed `r C$seed`) is the same on every rung, so the ladder is monotone in
+`q` by construction. The forecast rung is **q = `r FC$q`**, chosen as the
+smallest multiple of 5 above the interpolated harm with 80 % power at the
+null's 5 % threshold; there `c1*` = `r .f(FC$c1_star, 3)` (the `"resample"`
+inversion at target 0.80), the predicted power is `r .f(.fr$det_rate, 4)`
+(MC SE `r .f(.fr$det_rate_se, 4)`) and the predicted null false-declaration
+rate at the same `c1*` is `r .f(.fn$det_rate, 4)` (`r .f(.fn$det_rate_se, 4)`).
+The forecast was locked in commit `c9cb0ca2` before any replicate was drawn;
+the measured cell is
+`r if (S2$measured_cell == "run1_posthoc") "Stage 2's run 1 (effect.threshold = 30, the driver's own) scored post hoc at c1\\*, which its direct run 2 at effect.threshold = c1\\* reproduced replicate for replicate" else "Stage 2's direct run 2 (effect.threshold = c1\\*)"`
+(`r S2$run2$agree_decl` / `r S2$power$n` declarations agree; `r S2$run2$memb_same` / `r S2$run2$both` joint winners identical).
